# Two broken operators in one pipeline give two errors; the rest of the tree is usable.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..39
  PIPELINE@0..38
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..15
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..15
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "a"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        EQ@12..13 "="
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        LITERAL@14..15
          LONG@14..15 "1"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PROJECT_OP@18..27
      IDENT@18..25 "project"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@26..27
        NAME_REF@26..27
          IDENT@26..27 "b"
    WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
    ERROR@28..29
      IDENT@28..29 "c"
    WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
    PIPE@30..31 "|"
    WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
    TAKE_OP@32..38
      IDENT@32..36 "take"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      LITERAL@37..38
        LONG@37..38 "5"
  WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:13
  |
1 | t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
  |             ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `a == 1`

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `c`
  --> query:1:29
  |
1 | t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
  |                             ^

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | where a == 1 | project b c | take 5
which still has errors:

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `c`
  --> fixed:1:30
  |
1 | t | where a == 1 | project b c | take 5
  |                              ^
